{
  "requirement": "[`Sources`](../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/sources/struct.Sources.html) supplies\nbuilt-in filesystem listing, reading, outlining, text search, and structural\nsearch. Construct it with the project directory:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::sources::Sources;\n\nlet sources = Sources::new(repository_root);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.sources.provider` says `Sources`, built with `Sources::new(root)`, supplies built-in filesystem listing, reading, outlining, text search and structural search. The tests cover each capability through the constructor.\n\n- **Construction:** `Sources::new(root.path())` is used in `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` and in `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]`.\n- **Listing:** the gitignore test calls `list` with `SourceScope::all()` and with the default scope. It asserts that those results are equal. It asserts that specific paths are present or absent, including `keep.txt`, `src/nested.txt` and `.visible`, and the ignored files, `skip/` and `.git/`.\n- **Reading:** the same test asserts that `read` fails for ignored files and succeeds for `.gitignore`.\n- **Outlining:** the gitignore test asserts that `parse` fails for ignored files. The structural test calls `parse` on `note.unknown` and on `visible.rs`. It asserts the fingerprint schemes (`plain-text-structural-v1` and `rust-structural-v1`) and that the plain-text outline has 3 items.\n- **Text search:** the gitignore test asserts 3 matches for a literal pattern and for a regex pattern. It asserts the `complete` flag. It asserts empty results for ignored scopes, for `.git` and for `..`, which errors. It also asserts that `./src/../src` scopes correctly.\n- **Structural search:** the structural test asserts match path, selector and excerpt. It asserts limits (0 gives incomplete, 1 gives complete), scope exclusion, per-language filtering (rust against python) and the error for `..`.\n- **Defaults on a provider:** the unit test `src/sources/tests.rs#fn[defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot]` checks that the default parse and search methods compose a provider's primitives. It uses a `Memory` provider, not `Sources`, so it supports the requirement only indirectly.\n\nI found no obligation in the requirement text that these tests leave unchecked. The requirement states no further behaviors, such as error cases or particular outputs. Those belong to the refining requirements that the tests also cite.",
